BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:summer-school-2026@netsec-cost.eu
DTSTAMP:20260801T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Stockholm:20260609T090000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Stockholm:20260611T180000
SUMMARY:NetSec Early-Career Scholars Summer School
DESCRIPTION:Three days of training and mentoring for early-career researchers in European security: research presentations\, individualised feedback from senior scholars\, and structured mentorship. Open to PhD candidates and post-docs (within one year of defence) in strategic studies and international security\, as well as SWAMOS / Euro-SWAMOS alumni.\n\nScientific Coordinators: Dr Silvia D'Amato\, Prof Chiara Ruffa.\n\nFull details: https://netsec-cost.eu/summer-school.html
LOCATION:Stockholm University\, Frescativägen 114 18\, Sweden
URL;VALUE=URI:https://netsec-cost.eu/summer-school.html
ORGANIZER;CN=NetSec Summer School:mailto:ecs.netsec@eiss-europa.com
CATEGORIES:Training School,NetSec
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:european-security-conference-2026@netsec-cost.eu
DTSTAMP:20260801T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Stockholm:20260611T080000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Stockholm:20260612T200000
SUMMARY:2026 European Security Studies Conference
DESCRIPTION:The flagship annual gathering of the NetSec community: an interdisciplinary conference on European defence and security open to academics\, policy-makers\, and practitioners. Held back-to-back with the Summer School so early-career scholars can join the wider conversation.\n\nChairpersons: Dr Julia Carver\, Dr Sanne Verschuren.\n\nLive programme: https://netsec-cost.eu/essc-2026.html\nRegistration: https://indico.eiss-europa.com/event/22/
LOCATION:Stockholm University\, Frescativägen\, 114 19 Stockholm\, Sweden
URL;VALUE=URI:https://netsec-cost.eu/essc-2026.html
CATEGORIES:Annual Conference,NetSec
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:policy-workshop-2026-09@netsec-cost.eu
DTSTAMP:20260801T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Stockholm:20260913T090000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Stockholm:20260913T180000
SUMMARY:NetSec Policy Workshop: Great Power Politics and the Future of Alliances
DESCRIPTION:A NetSec Working Group 2 policy workshop on great power politics and the future of alliances\, convening scholars and policy practitioners to examine how alliance politics is evolving under intensifying great power competition\, and what the implications are for European security.\n\nAccommodation in Ankara and all meals are provided by Bilkent University and the Royal Danish Defence College. NetSec plans to reimburse accepted participants' travel costs through COST Action NetSec up to a maximum of €700 per participant\, pending a decision by NetSec's Management Committee.\n\nApplications close 15 August 2026. Full details and the application form: https://netsec-cost.eu/policy-workshop-2026.html
LOCATION:Bilkent University\, Ankara\, Türkiye
URL;VALUE=URI:https://netsec-cost.eu/policy-workshop-2026.html
CATEGORIES:Policy workshop,NetSec
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mc-plenary-2026-09@netsec-cost.eu
DTSTAMP:20260801T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Stockholm:20260918T090000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Stockholm:20260918T180000
SUMMARY:Inaugural NetSec Management Committee plenary
DESCRIPTION:The Action's first formal Management Committee plenary\, bringing together the MC representatives from the participating COST Member countries to align on workstreams\, confirm Working Group leadership for the coming cycle\, and elect any remaining roles. Followed by a Core Group working session.\n\nThe date is not yet confirmed. This entry is provisional and will be updated once the Action announces it.\n\nAccess is restricted to MC representatives\, Working Group leads\, and invited observers.
LOCATION:To be confirmed
URL;VALUE=URI:https://netsec-cost.eu/#events
CATEGORIES:MC Plenary,NetSec
STATUS:TENTATIVE
END:VEVENT
